--- TMT standard functions ---

--( Reading file in text mode, utf8
    Args: "File"::text
    Return: text )--
This is a tale "Read File" of kind text in wich "File" of kind text.
So it begins.
    There was an "Output" of kind text that should listen to the meaning of "File";
    If _$"ERROR"_ equals to _$"FILE READ ERROR"_; then
        Tell error `Could not read file '$"File"': $"ERROR MESSAGE"\n`.
        Quit _$"ERROR"_  -- Builtin variable ERROR is a number=u8
    That's it.
    Hand out the meaning of "Output".
The end.

--( Writing to file in text mode, utf8
    Args: "File"::text, "Text"::text
    Return: nil )--
This is a tale "Write File" in wich "File" of kind text, "Text" of kind text.
So it begins.
    Tell "File" the meaning of "Text".
    If _$"ERROR"_ equals to _$"FILE WRITE ERROR"_; then
        Tell error `Could not write to file '$"File"': $"ERROR MESSAGE"\n`.
        Quit _$"ERROR"_
    That's it.
The end.
